## Goal
Make the "not downloaded" error from iCloud sync say which step failed, so the user can tell what went wrong when an offloaded rules file can't be used.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
In `internal/sync/offload.go`, the base `ErrNotDownloaded` message is now generic ("not downloaded to this Mac; nothing changed"). It no longer claims a download started or suggests retrying. Each failure site in `ensureLocal` wraps it with its own reason in parentheses:
- download unsupported on this system
- the download could not start (with the underlying error)
- the download started but did not finish in time, with the retry-in-a-minute hint attached only here.

The previous base text was misleading, because it said "download started" even when it never started or was unsupported. The sentinel is still wrapped with `%w`, so `errors.Is` checks keep working.

